# RETRACTION: an earlier version of this header (written 2026-10-02 during the
# Section 16.3 audit) claimed MeshChatX was NOT installed here. That was WRONG.
# The audit searched for an "ao-field" unit, found none, and inferred the
# software was absent. MeshChatX actually runs under its own unit namespace:
#
#   systemctl --user status reticulum-meshchatx.service
#     active (running) since 2026-10-01 15:08:35 PDT, 17 processes
#   systemctl --user list-units  also shows reticulum-meshchatx-watchdog.timer
#   ExecStart=~/Applications/meshchatx-native/ReticulumMeshChatX --headless \
#             --host 127.0.0.1 --port 18000 \
#             --reticulum-config-dir ~/.reticulum \
#             --storage-dir ~/.reticulum-meshchatx
#
# WHERE THE REAL LOG IS:
#   ~/.reticulum-meshchatx/logs/meshchatx.log      3.4 MB, actively written
#   ~/.reticulum-meshchatx/logs/meshchatx.log.1    5.2 MB rotation
#   journald: journalctl --user -u reticulum-meshchatx.service  (19332 lines)
#
# The application writes that log itself, into its own storage dir, because
# --storage-dir is where it keeps state (identities, session secret, mbtiles).
# That directory is 907 MB of live application data and is NOT relocated to
# /ALWAYSON/logs/. Doing so would move user data, not just logs.
#
# This file is a POINTER, not a second writer. Do not append events here and do
# not let anything else write to the application's log -- two writers on one
# file interleave badly and the app holds the handle.
#
# Do not fabricate entries to make this look "regularly updated".
